<p>You can also control the <a href=3D"https://platform.openai.com/docs/gui=
des/tools-web-search">web search tool</a> without granting full network acc=
ess to spawned commands. Codex defaults to using a web search cache to acce=
ss results. The cache is an OpenAI-maintained index of web results, so cach=
ed mode returns pre-indexed results instead of fetching live pages. This re=
duces exposure to prompt injection from arbitrary live content, but you sho=
uld still treat web results as untrusted. If you are using <code>--yolo</co=
de> or another <a href=3D"https://developers.openai.com/codex/agent-approva=
ls-security#common-sandbox-and-approval-combinations">full access sandbox s=
etting</a>, web search defaults to live results. Use <code>--search</code> =
or set <code>web_search =3D "live"</code> to allow live browsing, or set it=
 to <code>"disabled"</code> to turn the tool off:</p>
