<p>In the default <code>workspace-write</code> sandbox policy, writable roo=
ts still include protected paths:</p>
<ul>
<li><code>&lt;writable_root&gt;/.git</code> is protected as read-only wheth=
er it appears as a directory or file.</li>
<li>If <code>&lt;writable_root&gt;/.git</code> is a pointer file (<code>git=
dir: ...</code>), the resolved Git directory path is also protected as read=
-only.</li>
<li><code>&lt;writable_root&gt;/.agents</code> is protected as read-only wh=
en it exists as a directory.</li>
<li><code>&lt;writable_root&gt;/.codex</code> is protected as read-only whe=
n it exists as a directory.</li>
<li>Protection is recursive, so everything under those paths is read-only.<=
/li>
</ul>
